1. Four pillars of an agent - 
    - LLM (Brain)
    - Context (Input)
    - Planning (How to get the result)
    - Tools 

2. Tools - In Agentic AI context A tool is a function or API that an agent can call during its 
reasoning loop to interact with the world.

Agent (LLM) → decides to use Tool → Tool executes → Result returned → Agent continues reasoning
Categories of Tools
Category	                        Examples
Information Retrieval	            Web search, vector DB lookup, RAG, file read
Action / Write	                    Send email, update DB, call REST API, write file
Computation	                        Code interpreter, calculator, data processing
Agent-to-Agent	                    Spawn sub-agent, call specialist agent
System / OS	                        Shell commands, browser control, GUI automation

3. The ReAct Loop (Reason + Act)

Observation	                        What the agent perceived after the last action.
Thought	                            The agent’s internal reasoning about what to do next.
Action	                            The tool call the agent decided to make.
Final Answer	                    The final output returned to the user.

